Third-party software:

This product depends on software distributed under separate, compatible
open-source licenses. Each dependency retains its own license.

THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt lists every third-party package a distributed build
carries, with the license text that package ships. It is generated from the
production dependency trees by scripts/licenses.mjs (`pnpm licenses`), it is
kept in the repository so it can be read without building anything, and the
packaged application ships it and shows it under "Open source licenses" in the
About screen.

Corral integrates with third-party AI providers, trackers, and repositories
using credentials supplied by the user (BYOK). Corral does not bundle any
proprietary provider binary, and does not embed any provider credentials.
Compliance with each provider's terms of service is the user's responsibility.
